/-! ## (A) THE BANKED JOIN CONTENT — the doubling-tear mirror multiplet + its quasi-degeneracy. -/

/-- ★★ THE BANKED DOUBLING TEAR (N277 `TL_sup_Sg_sup_TR_eq_top`, re-exported): the matter carrier's
    imaginary part splits into the un-doubled triplet `TL`, the doubling-axis singlet `Sg`, and the
    DOUBLED (mirror) triplet `TR` — `TL ⊔ Sg ⊔ TR = ⊤`. Forced by the terminal `O ℚ = CD (H ℚ)`. -/
theorem matter_doubling_tear : Phys.Algebra.TL ⊔ Phys.Algebra.Sg ⊔ Phys.Algebra.TR = ⊤ :=
  TL_sup_Sg_sup_TR_eq_top

/-- ★★ THE QUASI-DEGENERACY (N277 `casimirOp_*`, welded): the banked su(2)_L Casimir acts as the SAME
    scalar `−8` on a generator of the un-doubled triplet `TL` (`u1M`) AND on a generator of the
    doubled mirror triplet `TR` (`e5I`), while it is `0` on the doubling-axis singlet `Sg` (`e4I`).
    EQUAL Casimir eigenvalue on the mirror pair IS the derived quasi-degeneracy (not measured). -/
theorem mirror_quasi_degenerate :
    casimirOp u1M = (-8 : ℚ) • u1M ∧ casimirOp e5I = (-8 : ℚ) • e5I ∧ casimirOp e4I = 0 :=
  ⟨casimirOp_u1I, casimirOp_e5I, casimirOp_e4I⟩

/-- THE MIRROR-MULTIPLET CENSUS as a derived counting fact of the banked doubled triplet `TR`: its
    dimension `finrank ℚ TR` cast into the derived ℝ. A DERIVED count, NOT a free `3`. -/
